1
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:10,718
A parabola has eccentricity one: every point is exactly as far from the focus as from the directrix.

2
00:00:10,718 --> 00:00:21,089
Put the focus at a, zero and the directrix at x equals minus a. Move P along the curve: the yellow and red lengths are always equal.

3
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:30,703
Write PS equals PM with the distance formula, square both sides, and almost everything cancels: y squared equals four a x.

4
00:00:30,703 --> 00:00:36,919
The chord through the focus, the latus rectum, has length four a, which is why the four is there.

5
00:00:38,133 --> 00:00:43,330
Swap or negate the variables and the parabola faces the other three ways.

6
00:00:43,330 --> 00:00:50,882
The variable that is squared tells you the axis: y squared opens sideways, x squared opens up or down.

7
00:00:50,882 --> 00:00:59,254
Move the vertex to h, k and everything moves with it; the focus is always a units from the vertex along the axis.

8
00:01:00,467 --> 00:01:03,822
Only y is squared, so the axis is horizontal.

9
00:01:04,033 --> 00:01:09,977
Complete the square in y: y minus four squared equals four times x minus one.

10
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:13,275
Vertex one, four, and a equals one.

11
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:20,259
The focus is one unit right of the vertex, the directrix one unit left: the y axis.

12
00:01:20,259 --> 00:01:21,406
Latus rectum four.

13
00:01:23,433 --> 00:01:24,841
A real parabola.

14
00:01:24,841 --> 00:01:33,916
A bridge cable spans eighty metres, the towers are twenty metres high, and the lowest point of the cable is four metres above the road.

15
00:01:33,916 --> 00:01:36,372
How high is the cable twenty metres from the middle?

16
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:41,615
Put the origin at the lowest point: x squared equals four a y.

17
00:01:41,615 --> 00:01:46,940
Each tower top is forty across and sixteen up, so four a is a hundred.

18
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:52,509
At twenty metres, y is four: four above the lowest point, eight above the road.

19
00:01:53,733 --> 00:01:54,872
Parabola tangents.

20
00:01:55,100 --> 00:02:02,244
The tangent at x one, y one is y y one equals two a times x plus x one: y equals x plus three.

21
00:02:02,467 --> 00:02:06,767
The normal has slope minus one: x plus y equals nine.

22
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:15,374
For y equals m x plus c to touch y squared equals four a x, c must equal a over m.

23
00:02:15,374 --> 00:02:19,132
Here four over two is two: it touches, at one, four.

24
00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:30,665
Tie a loop of string to two pins and pull it tight with a pencil: you draw an ellipse.

25
00:02:30,665 --> 00:02:32,618
The two pins are the foci.

26
00:02:32,618 --> 00:02:39,615
However the pencil moves, the two distances add up to the same length, two a, the major axis.

27
00:02:39,833 --> 00:02:52,556
From the focus directrix rule with e less than one, the algebra gives x squared over a squared plus y squared over b squared equals one, where b squared is a squared times one minus e squared.

28
00:02:52,556 --> 00:02:56,879
So e is root of one minus b squared over a squared.

29
00:02:56,879 --> 00:03:06,808
The foci are at plus or minus a e, the directrices at plus or minus a over e, and the latus rectum is two b squared over a.

30
00:03:08,033 --> 00:03:09,233
A common slip.

31
00:03:09,233 --> 00:03:13,673
The foci always lie on the axis with the larger denominator.

32
00:03:13,673 --> 00:03:19,601
If the bigger number is under y squared, the ellipse is tall, and its foci are on the y axis.

33
00:03:20,833 --> 00:03:21,723
Read the ellipse.

34
00:03:22,067 --> 00:03:26,183
Divide by two twenty five: a is five, b is three.

35
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:34,132
e is four fifths, so the foci are at plus or minus four and the directrices at plus or minus twenty five over four.

36
00:03:34,333 --> 00:03:39,483
Major axis ten, minor six, latus rectum three point six.

37
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:42,503
An untidy one.

38
00:03:42,733 --> 00:03:46,844
Complete both squares, adding sixteen and nine to the right.

39
00:03:47,067 --> 00:03:48,532
Divide by thirty six.

40
00:03:48,733 --> 00:03:58,514
Centre two, minus one; a three, b two; e root five over three; and the foci root five either side of the centre.

41
00:04:00,533 --> 00:04:02,443
The T equals zero rule again.

42
00:04:02,667 --> 00:04:11,484
Tangent: x x one over a squared plus y y one over b squared equals one: three x plus five y equals twenty five.

43
00:04:11,700 --> 00:04:16,636
Normal: twenty five x minus fifteen y equals twenty seven.

44
00:04:16,636 --> 00:04:21,139
Slopes minus three fifths and five thirds: perpendicular.

45
00:04:26,733 --> 00:04:31,917
A hyperbola has eccentricity bigger than one, and comes in two branches.

46
00:04:31,917 --> 00:04:36,344
For an ellipse the distances to the foci add to a constant.

47
00:04:36,344 --> 00:04:39,853
For a hyperbola, their difference is constant: two a.

48
00:04:40,067 --> 00:04:55,655
The same algebra as the ellipse, but now one minus e squared is negative, and the plus sign becomes a minus: x squared over a squared minus y squared over b squared equals one, with b squared equal to a squared times e squared minus one.

49
00:04:55,655 --> 00:05:06,488
Far out, the branches hug two straight lines, the asymptotes, y equals plus or minus b over a x: the diagonals of the a by b box.

50
00:05:07,700 --> 00:05:09,668
Keep the two relations apart.

51
00:05:09,668 --> 00:05:14,186
For the ellipse, a squared e squared is a squared minus b squared.

52
00:05:14,186 --> 00:05:16,946
For the hyperbola, it is plus.

53
00:05:16,946 --> 00:05:18,756
Name the curve before you compute e.

54
00:05:19,967 --> 00:05:21,066
Read the hyperbola.

55
00:05:21,267 --> 00:05:24,619
Divide by one forty four: a four, b three.

56
00:05:24,833 --> 00:05:31,852
e is five quarters, foci at plus or minus five, directrices at plus or minus sixteen fifths.

57
00:05:32,067 --> 00:05:41,300
Vertices at plus or minus four, latus rectum four point five, and asymptotes three x plus or minus four y equals zero.

58
00:05:43,300 --> 00:05:45,289
The same rule, with a minus sign.

59
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:49,294
Tangent: five x minus four y equals sixteen.

60
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:54,163
Normal: sixteen x plus twenty y equals one two five.

61
00:05:54,163 --> 00:05:58,403
Slopes five quarters and minus four fifths: perpendicular.

62
00:06:00,433 --> 00:06:12,922
Here is the whole unit in one table: the standard equation, the eccentricity, the foci, the condition of tangency and the tangent at a point, for each of the four curves.

63
00:06:12,922 --> 00:06:15,768
Roughly a third of the marks in this unit are read straight off it.

64
00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:18,970
Pause and think.

65
00:06:26,267 --> 00:06:31,103
Exactly one: every point is as far from the focus as from the directrix.

66
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:34,026
One more.

67
00:06:34,026 --> 00:06:35,708
Which denominator is larger?

68
00:06:42,600 --> 00:06:45,336
Zero, plus or minus four.

69
00:06:45,336 --> 00:06:53,761
The larger denominator, twenty five, is under y squared, so the foci are on the y axis, root of twenty five minus nine away.

70
00:06:55,933 --> 00:06:57,002
Quick recap.

71
00:06:57,002 --> 00:07:02,263
One rule, PS equals e times PM, gives all four conics.

72
00:07:02,263 --> 00:07:07,536
The circle's centre and radius from the general form, and the tangency condition.

73
00:07:07,536 --> 00:07:13,942
The parabola, ellipse and hyperbola with their foci, directrices and latus recta.

74
00:07:13,942 --> 00:07:17,340
And the tangent at a point, by the T equals zero rule.

75
00:07:21,533 --> 00:07:23,305
That was conic sections.

76
00:07:23,305 --> 00:07:28,397
Next, product of vectors: the scalar and vector products and what they measure.

77
00:07:28,397 --> 00:07:28,990
See you there.

